      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Darlington Academy, erected in 1836, once served as a popular school for Harford County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darlington%2C_Maryland",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Every October, the town hosts an apple festival on the first Saturday that draws nearly 60,000 visitors.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darlington%2C_Maryland",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Harford County’s Celebration Trail, launched for America’s 250th birthday, guides visitors through 63 historic sites, including those in Darlington.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.harfordcountymd.gov/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In the 19th century, Darlington was a bustling stagecoach stop where traffic from the Susquehanna and Tidewater Canal flowed through.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darlington%2C_Maryland",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The 1928 construction of Conowingo Dam made crossing the Susquehanna River easier for Darlington residents.",
